        "original_id": "4ec5a5a8-7a83-52d2-a4b1-5a7e9f10f5c0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: HeroClix, Attacktix, Street Fighter\n- Companies: Capcom\n- Systems: Clix system\n- Topics: collectible miniatures games, fighting video game franchises, superhero comic book universes\n\nFacts:\n- Street Fighter is a fighting video game franchise developed and published by Capcom.\n- HeroClix is a collectible miniatures game that uses the Clix system and centers on superhero comic book worlds, especially the Marvel and DC Comics universes.\n- In HeroClix, players build teams of heroes, villains, or characters from video game series including Street Fighter, Gears of War, and Halo, and battle turn by turn on grid maps based on storyline locations.\n- Attacktix has been compared to HeroClix.",
